infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title The life of one row's update under MVCC
  desc A version is born on UPDATE, kept alive by an active snapshot, and only then reclaimed
  sequences
    - label A starts — gets snapshot
      desc Transaction A begins and is tagged with a snapshot frozen at this moment.
    - label A reads v1
      desc A reads the row at version v1 — the version stamped before A started.
    - label B updates — creates v2
      desc Transaction B updates the row, writing a new version v2 and marking v1 dead.
    - label B commits
      desc v2 becomes the latest version visible to any new snapshot.
    - label A still reads v1
      desc A keeps seeing v1; its snapshot predates v2, so neither waits.
    - label VACUUM reclaims v1
      desc Once no snapshot needs v1, VACUUM marks its space reusable.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
